<?xml version="1.0"?>
<rdf:RDF xmlns="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro#"
     xml:base="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro"
     xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"
     xmlns:ns1="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/"
     xmlns:ns2="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/"
     xmlns:ns3="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heao/"
     xmlns:ns4="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/rheo/"
     xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
     xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
     xmlns:xml="http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace"
     xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
     xmlns:foaf="http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/"
     xmlns:prov="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#"
     xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
     xmlns:skos="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#"
     xmlns:vann="http://purl.org/vocab/vann/"
     xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/"
     xmlns:oboInOwl="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#">
    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro">
        <owl:versionIRI rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/0.2.0/heiro.owl"/>
        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Baines D, Ashley M. Health Economics Institutions and Rules Ontology (HEIRO), version 0.1.0, for BioPortal. Intelligent Parameters Ltd; 2026. https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/0.2.0/heiro.owl. Licence CC BY 4.0.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <dcterms:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-10-19</dcterms:created>
        <dcterms:creator rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9502-4678"/>
        <dcterms:creator rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731"/>
        <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">HEIRO, the Health Economics Institutions and Rules Ontology, holds the institutions of health economics and health technology assessment in Darrin Baines&apos;s sense, the rules that set the options actors have, and keeps them apart from the organizations that issue and apply them. A body is an organization that bears an institutional role, such as a health technology assessment role. Its rules are stated in guidance documents, each a lineage of dated guidance versions, and every rule HEIRO records names the provision, the version and the body it comes from and the period in which it is in force. A guidance version check record says when, and from which copy, a version was found to be current, so that any page, formula or rule that cites a guidance version can be found and flagged when a newer version exists. HEIRO reuses RHEO for organizations, geographic areas, decision threshold, discounting and perspective specifications, HEAO for decision modifier rules and value types, OHEO for reference case requirements and profiles, and PROV-O for revision and derivation. Every relationship it makes to another ontology of the family is typed with one of the five linking kinds of HEAO 0.2.0.</dcterms:description>
        <dcterms:issued rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-10-19</dcterms:issued>
        <dcterms:license rdf:resource="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"/>
        <dcterms:publisher>Intelligent Parameters Ltd</dcterms:publisher>
        <dcterms:title xml:lang="en">Health Economics Institutions and Rules Ontology (HEIRO)</dcterms:title>
        <vann:preferredNamespacePrefix>heiro</vann:preferredNamespacePrefix>
        <vann:preferredNamespaceUri>https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_</vann:preferredNamespaceUri>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This file, heiro-0.2.0-merged.owl, is the file for BioPortal. It holds HEIRO&apos;s core terms and its institutional register (bodies, jurisdictions, guidance documents, versions, provisions and rules), merged by ROBOT with a BOT extract of the outside terms HEIRO uses from RHEO 0.4.0, HEAO 0.2.0, OHEO 0.3.0 and BFO 2020, so that BioPortal lists HEIRO&apos;s own terms. The records generated from the healtheconomics.wiki, institutional perspective records and guidance citation records, are in heiro-wiki.owl and are left out of this file. First release, status alpha, unreviewed.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heao"/>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo"/>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heo"/>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heto"/>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/oheo"/>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/rheo"/>
        <owl:versionInfo>0.2.0 (alpha)</owl:versionInfo>
        <foaf:homepage rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro"/>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


