        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_9000005"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heao/HEAO_0000052"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The figure this rule states is a HEAO discount rate, so a valuation that applies it can be typed by HEAO.</rdfs:comment>
        <ns3:HEAO_9000001 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heao/HEAO_4000001"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000177 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000177">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_0000010"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000004 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000148"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000005 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/economic-evaluation-2#pmg36-4_5_2</ns1:HEIRO_2000005>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000006>4.5.2</ns1:HEIRO_2000006>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000007>Alternative analyses using rates of 1.5% for both costs and health effects may be presented alongside the reference-case analysis, in specific circumstances.</ns1:HEIRO_2000007>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PMG36 section 4.5.2, version of 13 October 2026</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000178 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000178">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_0000010"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000004 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000148"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000005 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/economic-evaluation-2#pmg36-4_5_3</ns1:HEIRO_2000005>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000006>4.5.3</ns1:HEIRO_2000006>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000007>The committee may consider analyses using a non-reference-case discount rate of 1.5% per year for both costs and health effects, if, in the committee&apos;s considerations, all of the following criteria are met: The technology is for people who would otherwise die or have a very severely impaired life. It is likely to restore them to full or near-full health. The benefits are likely to be sustained over a very long period.</ns1:HEIRO_2000007>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PMG36 section 4.5.3, version of 13 October 2026</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000179 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000179">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_0000011"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/rheo/RHEO_0000072"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000005 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000180"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000015 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000001"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000030>2026-10-13</ns1:HEIRO_2000030>
        <ns4:RHEO_2000027>costs of the NHS and personal social services, and all relevant health effects on patients and, when relevant, other people such as carers</ns4:RHEO_2000027>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Stated in PMG36, in the versions of 13 October 2026.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">NICE reference-case perspective, the NHS and personal social services for costs and all relevant health effects</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000180 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000180">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_0000010"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000004 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000148"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000005 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/economic-evaluation-2#pmg36-4_2_7</ns1:HEIRO_2000005>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000006>4.2.7</ns1:HEIRO_2000006>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000007>For the reference case, the perspective on outcomes should be all relevant health effects, whether for patients or, when relevant, other people (mainly carers). The perspective adopted on costs should be that of the NHS and PSS.</ns1:HEIRO_2000007>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PMG36 section 4.2.7, version of 13 October 2026</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000181 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000181">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_0000011"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/oheo/OHEO_0000328"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000005 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000182"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000015 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000001"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000013>Cost-effectiveness (cost-utility) analysis</ns1:HEIRO_2000013>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000030>2026-10-13</ns1:HEIRO_2000030>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Stated in PMG36, in the versions of 13 October 2026.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">NICE rule that health effects are expressed in QALYs</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000182 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000182">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_0000010"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000004 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000148"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000005 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/economic-evaluation-2#pmg36-4_2_14</ns1:HEIRO_2000005>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000006>4.2.14</ns1:HEIRO_2000006>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000007>Cost-effectiveness (specifically cost-utility) analysis is used to determine if differences in expected costs between technologies can be justified in terms of changes in expected health effects. Health effects should be expressed in terms of quality-adjusted life years (QALYs) .</ns1:HEIRO_2000007>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PMG36 section 4.2.14, version of 13 October 2026</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000183 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000183">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_0000011"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_0000012"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000005 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000184"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000005 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000253"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000005 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000254"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000015 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000001"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000023 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_4000014"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000024 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_4000017"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000030>2026-10-13</ns1:HEIRO_2000030>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Stated in PMG36, in the versions of 13 October 2026.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">NICE comparator rule, the technologies that are established practice in the NHS, including generics, biosimilars and technologies recommended after the severity modifier</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000184 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000184">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_0000010"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000004 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000148"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000005 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/the-scope-2#pmg36-2_2_12</ns1:HEIRO_2000005>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000006>2.2.12</ns1:HEIRO_2000006>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000007>The scope identifies all potentially relevant comparators that are established practice in the NHS. It considers issues likely to be discussed by the committee when selecting the most appropriate comparator. At this stage of the evaluation, identifying comparators should be inclusive.</ns1:HEIRO_2000007>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PMG36 section 2.2.12, version of 13 October 2026</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000185 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000185">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_0000010"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000004 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000148"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000005 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/the-scope-2#pmg36-2_2_15</ns1:HEIRO_2000005>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000006>2.2.15</ns1:HEIRO_2000006>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000007>Technologies that NICE has recommended with managed access are not considered established practice in the NHS and are not considered suitable comparators.</ns1:HEIRO_2000007>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PMG36 section 2.2.15, version of 13 October 2026</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000186 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000186">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_0000011"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/rheo/RHEO_0000117"/>
        <ns3:HEAO_1000026 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000261"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000005 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000187"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000005 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000219"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000015 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000001"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000013>Technology appraisals. Below this most plausible ICER the decision is normally based on the cost-effectiveness estimate</ns1:HEIRO_2000013>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000028>2026-03-31</ns1:HEIRO_2000028>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000030>2026-03-31</ns1:HEIRO_2000030>
        <ns4:RHEO_2000001 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">25000.0</ns4:RHEO_2000001>
        <ns4:RHEO_2000002>GBP per QALY gained</ns4:RHEO_2000002>
        <ns4:RHEO_2000003>GBP</ns4:RHEO_2000003>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Stated in PMG36, in the versions of 31 March 2026, 13 October 2026.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">NICE most plausible ICER of 25,000 pounds per QALY gained for technology appraisals</rdfs:label>
        <ns1:HEIRO_9000004 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/HEMO_5000196"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_9000004 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/HEMO_5000213"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_9000005 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heao/HEAO_0000094"/>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000186"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heao/HEAO_1000026"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000261"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The version of 31 March 2026 replaced the threshold values of the version of 17 December 2025, as its update information says.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000186"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heao/HEAO_1000026"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000261"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The version of 31 March 2026 replaced the threshold values of the version of 17 December 2025, as its update information says.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000186"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_9000004"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/HEMO_5000196"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The HEMO formula Incremental net monetary benefit takes the figures of this rule as inputs, since HEMO keeps policy figures out of its formulas.</rdfs:comment>
        <ns3:HEAO_9000001 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heao/HEAO_4000003"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000186"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_9000004"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/HEMO_5000213"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The HEMO formula Incremental net health benefit at threshold k takes the figures of this rule as inputs, since HEMO keeps policy figures out of its formulas.</rdfs:comment>
        <ns3:HEAO_9000001 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heao/HEAO_4000003"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000186"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_9000005"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heao/HEAO_0000094"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The figure this rule states is a HEAO adopted threshold value, so a valuation that applies it can be typed by HEAO.</rdfs:comment>
        <ns3:HEAO_9000001 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heao/HEAO_4000001"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000187 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000187">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_0000010"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000004 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000148"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000005 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2#pmg36-6_3_4</ns1:HEIRO_2000005>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000006>6.3.4</ns1:HEIRO_2000006>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000007>Below a most plausible ICER of £25,000 per QALY gained, or £100,000 per QALY gained for highly specialised technologies, the decision to recommend a technology is normally based on the cost-effectiveness estimate and the acceptability of a technology as an effective use of NHS resources. When the estimated ICERs are less than £25,000 per QALY gained, or £100,000 per QALY gained for highly specialised technologies, and the committee decides that the technology should not be recommended, the committee will make specific reference to its view on the plausibility of the inputs to the economic modelling, or the certainty around the estimated ICER, or both. This might be affected, for example, by sensitivity analysis or limitations to the generalisability of findings about effectiveness.</ns1:HEIRO_2000007>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PMG36 section 6.3.4, version of 13 October 2026</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000188 -->

