    <!-- https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000218 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000218">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_0000010"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000004 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000172"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000005 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://pbac.pbs.gov.au/section-3a/3a-1-overview-and-rationale-of-economic-evaluation.html</ns1:HEIRO_2000005>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000006>3A.1.5</ns1:HEIRO_2000006>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000007>annual (compounding) rate of 5% per year for all costs and health outcomes that occur</ns1:HEIRO_2000007>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PBAC Guidelines section 3A.1.5, version of September 2016</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000219 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000219">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_0000010"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000004 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000145"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000005 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://web.archive.org/web/20260618195253id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2</ns1:HEIRO_2000005>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000006>6.3.4</ns1:HEIRO_2000006>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000007>Below a most plausible ICER of £25,000 per QALY gained, or £100,000 per QALY gained for highly specialised technologies, the decision to recommend a technology is normally based on the cost-effectiveness estimate and the acceptability of a technology as an effective use of NHS resources. When the estimated ICERs are less than £25,000 per QALY gained, or £100,000 per QALY gained for highly specialised technologies, and the committee decides that the technology should not be recommended, the committee will make specific reference to its view on the plausibility of the inputs to the economic modelling, or the certainty around the estimated ICER, or both. This might be affected, for example, by sensitivity analysis or limitations to the generalisability of findings about effectiveness.</ns1:HEIRO_2000007>
        <ns2:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">Read in an archived copy of the page, https://web.archive.org/web/20260618195253id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2</ns2:IAO_0000116>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PMG36 section 6.3.4, version of 31 March 2026</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000221 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000221">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_0000010"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000004 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000145"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000005 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://web.archive.org/web/20260618195253id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2</ns1:HEIRO_2000005>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000006>6.3.7</ns1:HEIRO_2000006>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000007>As the ICER for a technology increases in the range of £25,000 to £35,000 per QALY gained, the committee&apos;s decisions about the acceptability of the technology as an effective use of NHS resources will make explicit reference to the relevant factors listed in section 6.3.5.</ns1:HEIRO_2000007>
        <ns2:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">Read in an archived copy of the page, https://web.archive.org/web/20260618195253id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2</ns2:IAO_0000116>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PMG36 section 6.3.7, version of 31 March 2026</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000222 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000222">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_0000010"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000004 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000145"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000005 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://web.archive.org/web/20260618195253id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2</ns1:HEIRO_2000005>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000006>6.3.8</ns1:HEIRO_2000006>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000007>Above a most plausible ICER of £35,000 per QALY gained or £100,000 per QALY gained for highly specialised technologies, the committee will need to identify an increasingly stronger case for supporting the technology as an effective use of NHS resources, considering the factors listed in sections 6.3.5 and 6.3.6.</ns1:HEIRO_2000007>
        <ns2:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">Read in an archived copy of the page, https://web.archive.org/web/20260618195253id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2</ns2:IAO_0000116>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PMG36 section 6.3.8, version of 31 March 2026</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


