        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_1000008"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000288"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Table A1 and appendix B replace figure 4.1. On 19 October 2026 the PMG36 page still showed the earlier wording.</rdfs:comment>
        <ns1:HEIRO_9000007 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_4000021"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000227 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000227">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_0000010"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000004 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000148"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000005 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/economic-evaluation-2#pmg36-4_2_2</ns1:HEIRO_2000005>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000006>4.2.2</ns1:HEIRO_2000006>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000007>Although the reference case specifies the methods preferred by NICE, it does not prevent the committee&apos;s consideration of non-reference-case analyses if appropriate. The key elements of analysis using the reference case are summarised in table 4.1.</ns1:HEIRO_2000007>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PMG36 section 4.2.2, version of 13 October 2026</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000228 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000228">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_0000010"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000004 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000148"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000005 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/economic-evaluation-2#pmg36-4_3_6</ns1:HEIRO_2000005>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000006>4.3.6</ns1:HEIRO_2000006>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000007>Given the need for consistency across evaluations, the EQ-5D measurement method is preferred to measure health-related quality of life in adults. Preference values from the EQ-5D should be applied to measurements of health-related quality of life to generate health-related utility values.</ns1:HEIRO_2000007>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PMG36 section 4.3.6, version of 13 October 2026</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000229 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000229">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_0000010"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000004 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000148"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000005 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/economic-evaluation-2#pmg36-4_3_8</ns1:HEIRO_2000005>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000006>4.3.8</ns1:HEIRO_2000006>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000007>If not available in the relevant clinical trials, EQ-5D data can be sourced from the literature. When taken from the literature, the methods for identifying the data should be systematic and transparent. Clearly explain the justification for choosing a particular data set. When more than 1 plausible set of EQ-5D data is available, sensitivity analyses should be done to show the effect of the alternative utility values.</ns1:HEIRO_2000007>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PMG36 section 4.3.8, version of 13 October 2026</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000230 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000230">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_0000010"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000004 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000148"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000005 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/economic-evaluation-2#pmg36-4_3_9</ns1:HEIRO_2000005>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000006>4.3.9</ns1:HEIRO_2000006>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000007>When EQ-5D data is not available, this data can be estimated by mapping other health-related quality-of-life measures or health-related benefits seen in the relevant clinical trials to EQ-5D. This is considered to be a departure from the reference case. The mapping function chosen should be based on data sets containing both health-related quality-of-life measures and its statistical properties. It should be fully described, its choice justified, and it should be adequately shown how well the function fits the data. Present sensitivity analyses to explore variation in using mapping algorithms on the outputs.</ns1:HEIRO_2000007>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PMG36 section 4.3.9, version of 13 October 2026</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000231 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000231">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_0000010"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000004 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000148"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000005 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/economic-evaluation-2#pmg36-4_3_12</ns1:HEIRO_2000005>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000006>4.3.12</ns1:HEIRO_2000006>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000007>A hierarchy of preferred health-related quality-of-life methods is presented in figure 4.1. Use figure 4.1 for guidance when the EQ-5D is not available or not appropriate.</ns1:HEIRO_2000007>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PMG36 section 4.3.12, version of 13 October 2026</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000232 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000232">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_0000010"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_1000004 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/HEIRO_5000148"/>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000005 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/economic-evaluation-2#pmg36-4_3_16</ns1:HEIRO_2000005>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000006>4.3.16</ns1:HEIRO_2000006>
        <ns1:HEIRO_2000007>The EQ-5D-5L is a new version of the EQ-5D, with 5 response levels. NICE does not recommend using the EQ-5D-5L value set for England published by Devlin et al. (2018). Companies, academic groups and others preparing evidence submissions for NICE should use the 3L value set for reference-case analyses. If data was gathered using the EQ-5D-5L descriptive system, utility values in reference-case analyses should be calculated by mapping the 5L descriptive system data onto the 3L value set. If analyses use data gathered using both EQ-5D-3L and EQ-5D-5L descriptive systems, the 3L value set should be used to derive all utility values, with 5L mapped onto 3L when needed. The mapping function developed by the Decision Support Unit (Hernández Alava et al. 2017), using the &apos;EEPRU dataset&apos; (Hernández Alava et al. 2020), should be used for reference-case analyses. We support sponsors of prospective clinical studies continuing to use the 5L version of the EQ-5D descriptive system to collect data on quality of life.</ns1:HEIRO_2000007>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PMG36 section 4.3.16, version of 13 October 2026</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


